Since we need to count numbers in a range $[num1, num2]$ satisfying a condition on digit sums, this is a classic Digit DP problem.
The number of good integers in $[num1, num2]$ is equal to the number of good integers in $[0, num2]$ minus the number of good integers in $[0, num1-1]$.
Alternatively, we can define a function `count(n, min_sum, max_sum)` that returns the number of integers $x$ such that $0 \le x \le n$ and $min\_sum \le \text{digit\_sum}(x) \le max\_sum$. Then the answer is `(count(num2, min_sum, max_sum) - count(num1_minus_1, min_sum, max_sum)) % MOD`.

